   "source": [
    "# Notebook 3: Comparing Predictions with Experimental Data\n\n## Learning Objectives\n\n1. Load experimental gene essentiality data\n2. Compare model predictions with experiments\n3. Calculate comparison metrics (precision, recall, accuracy)\n4. Visualize agreements and disagreements\n5. Interpret discrepancies between model and experiments\n\n## Why Compare with Experiments?\n\nModel validation is critical:\n- **Validate** the model's predictive power\n- **Identify** model limitations\n- **Refine** the model based on discrepancies\n- **Guide** experimental design\n\n---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Import necessary libraries for data analysis and visualization\nimport pandas as pd  # For data manipulation and loading CSV files\nimport numpy as np   # For numerical operations and calculations\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt  # For creating plots and charts\nimport seaborn as sns  # For statistical data visualization\nimport os  # For operating system interactions (file paths, etc.)\n\n# Set pandas display options to show all columns when printing DataFrames\npd.set_option('display.max_columns', None)\n\n# Set the default plotting style to 'seaborn' for better looking plots\nplt.style.use('seaborn-v0_8')\n\n# Set the color palette to 'husl' which provides distinct, evenly spaced colors\nsns.set_palette(\"husl\")\n\n# Print a confirmation message to verify successful loading\nprint(\"Libraries loaded successfully!\")"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Load Model Predictions\n\nWe'll load the essentiality results from Notebook 2."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Load predicted essentiality results\npredicted_df = pd.read_csv('../results/essentiality/gene_essentiality_default_medium.csv')\n\nprint(f\"Loaded {len(predicted_df)} gene predictions\")\nprint(f\"Essential (predicted): {predicted_df['is_essential'].sum()}\")\n\n# Get set of predicted essential genes\npredicted_essential = set(predicted_df[predicted_df['is_essential']]['gene_id'])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Load Experimental Data\n\n**Note**: You need to provide experimental data in CSV format with columns:\n- `gene_id`: Gene identifier\n- `is_essential`: True/False or 1/0\n\nFor this demonstration, we'll show how to load and use such data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Example: Load experimental data\n# experimental_df = pd.read_csv('../data/experimental/gene_essentiality_experimental.csv')\n# experimental_essential = set(experimental_df[experimental_df['is_essential']]['gene_id'])\n\n# For demonstration, we'll create a mock dataset\n# In real use, replace this with actual experimental data\nimport random\nrandom.seed(42)\n\n# Simulate experimental data with some overlap with predictions\nexperimental_essential = set(random.sample(list(predicted_essential), \n                                          int(len(predicted_essential) * 0.7)))\nexperimental_essential.update(random.sample(\n    list(set(predicted_df['gene_id']) - predicted_essential),\n    int(len(predicted_df) * 0.05)\n))\n\nprint(f\"\\nExperimental essential genes: {len(experimental_essential)}\")\nprint(\"\\n\u26a0 Note: Using simulated data for demonstration.\")\nprint(\"   Replace with real experimental data for actual analysis.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Calculate Comparison Metrics\n\nWe'll calculate:\n- **True Positives (TP)**: Correctly predicted essential\n- **False Positives (FP)**: Predicted essential but not essential\n- **True Negatives (TN)**: Correctly predicted non-essential\n- **False Negatives (FN)**: Predicted non-essential but actually essential\n\nFrom these we calculate:\n- **Precision**: TP / (TP + FP) - How many predicted essentials are correct?\n- **Recall (Sensitivity)**: TP / (TP + FN) - How many actual essentials did we find?\n- **Accuracy**: (TP + TN) / Total - Overall correctness"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Calculate overlap\ntrue_positives = predicted_essential & experimental_essential\nfalse_positives = predicted_essential - experimental_essential\nfalse_negatives = experimental_essential - predicted_essential\ntrue_negatives = (set(predicted_df['gene_id']) - predicted_essential - experimental_essential)\n\nTP = len(true_positives)\nFP = len(false_positives)\nFN = len(false_negatives)\nTN = len(true_negatives)\n\nprint(\"Confusion Matrix:\")\nprint(\"=\" * 40)\nprint(f\"True Positives (TP):   {TP}\")\nprint(f\"False Positives (FP):  {FP}\")\nprint(f\"False Negatives (FN):  {FN}\")\nprint(f\"True Negatives (TN):   {TN}\")\n\n# Calculate metrics\nprecision = TP / (TP + FP) if (TP + FP) > 0 else 0\nrecall = TP / (TP + FN) if (TP + FN) > 0 else 0\naccuracy = (TP + TN) / (TP + TN + FP + FN) if (TP + TN + FP + FN) > 0 else 0\nf1_score = 2 * (precision * recall) / (precision + recall) if (precision + recall) > 0 else 0\n\nprint(\"\\nPerformance Metrics:\")\nprint(\"=\" * 40)\nprint(f\"Precision: {precision:.3f} ({precision*100:.1f}%)\")\nprint(f\"Recall:    {recall:.3f} ({recall*100:.1f}%)\")\nprint(f\"Accuracy:  {accuracy:.3f} ({accuracy*100:.1f}%)\")\nprint(f\"F1 Score:  {f1_score:.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: Visualize with Venn Diagram"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create Venn diagram\nplt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\nvenn2([predicted_essential, experimental_essential], \n      set_labels=('Model Prediction', 'Experimental'))\nplt.title(f'Essential Gene Comparison\\n'\n          f'TP={TP}, FP={FP}, FN={FN}, Precision={precision:.2f}, Recall={recall:.2f}')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5: Examine Discrepancies\n\nLet's look at genes where model and experiment disagree."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"False Positives (predicted essential, but not in experiments):\")\nprint(f\"Total: {len(false_positives)}\")\nif len(false_positives) > 0:\n    print(\"First 10 examples:\")\n    for i, gene in enumerate(list(false_positives)[:10]):\n        print(f\"  {i+1}. {gene}\")\n\nprint(\"\\nFalse Negatives (not predicted, but essential in experiments):\")\nprint(f\"Total: {len(false_negatives)}\")\nif len(false_negatives) > 0:\n    print(\"First 10 examples:\")\n    for i, gene in enumerate(list(false_negatives)[:10]):\n        print(f\"  {i+1}. {gene}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6: Growth Ratio Analysis\n\nLet's see how growth ratios differ for correctly vs incorrectly predicted genes."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Create categories\npredicted_df['prediction_type'] = 'TN'  # Default\n\npredicted_df.loc[\n    predicted_df['gene_id'].isin(true_positives), 'prediction_type'\n] = 'TP'\n\npredicted_df.loc[\n    predicted_df['gene_id'].isin(false_positives), 'prediction_type'\n] = 'FP'\n\npredicted_df.loc[\n    predicted_df['gene_id'].isin(false_negatives), 'prediction_type'\n] = 'FN'\n\n# Plot distributions\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))\n\nfor pred_type in ['TP', 'FP', 'FN', 'TN']:\n    subset = predicted_df[predicted_df['prediction_type'] == pred_type]\n    if len(subset) > 0:\n        ax.hist(subset['growth_ratio'], bins=30, alpha=0.5, label=f'{pred_type} (n={len(subset)})')\n\nax.set_xlabel('Growth Ratio (knockout/wildtype)')\nax.set_ylabel('Frequency')\nax.set_title('Growth Ratio Distribution by Prediction Type')\nax.legend()\nax.axvline(x=0.01, color='red', linestyle='--', label='Threshold')\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Summary\n\nIn this notebook, you learned:\n\n1. \u2713 How to load and structure experimental data\n2. \u2713 How to compare model predictions with experiments\n3. \u2713 How to calculate validation metrics (precision, recall, accuracy)\n4. \u2713 How to visualize agreements and discrepancies\n5. \u2713 How to interpret differences between model and reality\n\n### Understanding Discrepancies:\n\n**False Positives** (predicted essential, but not experimental) may indicate:\n- Model missing alternative pathways\n- Incorrect GPR associations\n- Medium differences between model and experiment\n\n**False Negatives** (experimental essential, not predicted) may indicate:\n- Missing reactions in the model\n- Incomplete model reconstruction\n- Regulatory effects not captured by FBA\n\n### Key Takeaways:\n\n- No model is perfect - validation helps identify gaps\n- Metabolic models are constantly refined based on new data\n- Combining computational and experimental approaches is powerful\n- Context matters - essentiality depends on growth conditions\n\n---"
   ]
  }
